p.src:
Add a third principle: gauge invariance. For the moment set $J^\mu=0$ and consider the free field. A gauge transformation is $A_\mu\longrightarrow A_\mu+\partial_\mu\chi.$ The field tensor does not change because mixed second derivatives commute: $\begin{aligned}
F_{\mu\nu}
&\longrightarrow
F_{\mu\nu}
+\partial_\mu\partial_\nu\chi
-\partial_\nu\partial_\mu\chi
\nonumber\\
&=F_{\mu\nu}.\end{aligned}$

