Differentiate: $\begin{aligned}
\frac{\partial\mathcal L_{\mathrm{EM}}}
{\partial A_{x,y}}
&=
-\left(A_{x,y}-A_{y,x}\right)
\nonumber\\
&=
F_{xy}.
\end{aligned}$ The board summarizes this with a minus sign attached to the tensor whose indices follow the board’s derivative ordering. With the course-wide definition , the invariant statement is $\frac{\partial\mathcal L_{\mathrm{EM}}}
{\partial(\partial_\mu A_\nu)}
=
-F^{\mu\nu}.$ For the example $\partial_yA_x$, this gives $-F^{yx}=F^{xy}$, precisely . Thus the apparent sign difference is only an index-order bookkeeping issue.

