The simplest local Lorentz scalar linear in both the current and the potential is $S_{\mathrm{int}}
=
-\int d^4x\,J^\mu A_\mu.$ The overall sign is conventional. The lecture jokes that the historical choice of electric-charge sign can ultimately be blamed on Benjamin Franklin; the real point is that one consistent sign convention must be used everywhere.

