The mismatch is not hidden. The calculation is retraced in real time; the required continuity equation is stated; and a member of the audience checks the equation and identifies the source sign. The conventionally consistent component equation is $\boxed{
\dot{\mathbf E}+\nabla\times\mathbf B=-\,\mathbf J,
}$ or $\dot{\mathbf E}
=
-\nabla\times\mathbf B-\mathbf J.$ Now equations  and  give $\begin{aligned}
\dot\rho
&=
\nabla\cdot
\left(-\nabla\times\mathbf B-\mathbf J\right)
\nonumber\\
&=
-\nabla\cdot\mathbf J,\end{aligned}$ which is exactly local charge conservation.

